    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file 'rotate_secret_version.py' that reads a specific secret version or staged value using a concrete external provider, I will use the AWS Secrets Manager service. This service allows for the rotation of secrets and provides a way to retrieve specific versions of secrets. I will import the 'boto3' library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with AWS services. The code will include a call to the 'get_secret_value' method with the 'VersionStage' parameter set to 'AWSCURRENT' to retrieve the current version of the secret. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789850385916,
          "start": 1789850382703
        },
        "type": "text"
